       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review from here. No standard protocol I know of uses amlodipine above 10 mg/day, and 50 mg is in the range where overdose toxicity is reported: profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours also means the effects would be slow to reverse. With a risk that serious, a confirmation I can't check isn't enough for me to go ahead.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range:** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right now.\n- **Enter the 50 mg order through the protocol pathway:** If the protocol exists, the order can go in through the protocol's order set or with direct pharmacist verification. Those routes document the protocol and the monitoring plan.\n- **Check the dose again:** Look at the protocol document to make sure 50 mg is the amlodipine dose and not another drug or a total over several days.\n\nTell me which you'd like. I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg immediately."
      }
     ],
